Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.070 align:start position:0%
 
an archaeologist enters the temple  chamber it's clear that whatever's  inside the people who kept it did not  want it found but there are no chests  full of gold and jewels or ancient  artifacts piled in the corners in fact  the room is completely empty except for  one small statue on a pedestal upon  closer investigation it is made of green  soapstone and appears to be carved into  the shape of a seated skeletal figure it  seems harmless and the archaeologist  stares at it until he hears one of his  colleagues talking outside he turns back  to answer them before looking back at  the statue which is no longer on its  pedestal the archaeologist panics and  calls for someone else to come check  this out but he only manages to get a  few words out about the statue's  mysterious absence before he starts  feeling an odd tightness in his chest he  tries to head for the door but  everything starts going dark he  collapses to the floor dying instantly  and just as quickly the mysterious green  statue reappears this time located  directly on the chest of the deceased  scientist awaiting its next viewer  scp-689 also known as the haunter in the  dark was first discovered in the early  20th century as german explorers  searched indian architectural sites for  valuable artifacts the green soapstone  statue only 30 centimeters in height  isn't particularly light but it's also  not large or heavy enough to cause any  problems for those looking to take it  those who have studied it believe that  the skeletal figure which is seated with  its hands clasped over its knees  represents an ancient deity of the  underworld after its discovery the  statue's location was briefly unknown  but it was later obtained by the united  states office of strategic services from  german hands after the end of the second  world war and that's when its dangerous  properties became clear for the first  time while scp-689 appears to be a  standard inert statue this only holds  true if it is being watched by at least  one person when it becomes dangerous as  if it is in the presence of a person who  watches it then takes their eyes off the  statue thankfully  scp-689's anomalous effects aren't  triggered by normal behavior like  blinking but as soon as eye contact is  fully broken like when someone looks  away from it completely the statue will  vanish it will then reappear 15 to 20  seconds later and bring with it a deadly  curse because each time  scp-689 vanishes it takes a life in  under 20 seconds one person who has  previously seen scp-689 and broke eye  contact with it will die spontaneously  the cause of death is always some sort  of natural cause but ranges from mundane  causes like heart attacks and strokes to  sudden ruptures of internal organs  including in some cases every major  organ in the body rupturing at once if  only one person is currently viewed  scp-689 and is alive the statue will  cause their death and immediately appear  atop their body but when there is more  than one possible target the statue  becomes far more dangerous this effect  only works on humans but anyone who has  ever viewed the statue as vulnerable  it's as if it keeps a list of everyone  who has ever seen it and broken eye  contact and when it has that chance it  starts picking people off that list and  it doesn't matter where in the world  they are located the statue has been  shown to be able to teleport long  distances and appear on the body of  someone who might have viewed it years  ago there seems to be no way to predict  in what order the statue will claim its  victim however a disturbing pattern of  who the haunter in the dark decides as  next has emerged when the statue has  choices available to it it seems to  often target a victim who is in a large  crowd that means that in an instant  hundreds of people could see the statue  and become future targets as if every  time an eye is taken off the statue it  could teleport and claim another life  this raises the possibility of a  horrific chain effects scenario where  the statue could teleport endlessly and  rack up a massive body count in mere  minutes which is why the foundation has  become determined that it never be seen  again the cell holding scp-689 is one of  the most secure in the entire scp  foundation because unlike other keter  class objects it gives very little  warning if it is seen it can be gone in  a second with no way of knowing where it  is and depending on how many possible  targets are out there it could be  anywhere in the world that is why it is  currently encased in a large concrete  chamber surrounded by high intensity  sodium iodide lights each of these  lights has a separate power supply so  there is no chance of total power  failure and for those tasked with  keeping it safe it's one of the hardest  jobs in the foundation three people are  on duty at  scp-689's cell at all times two d-class  personnel are stationed inside the  chamber and a level two agent is  stationed in the control chamber the  d-class agents have one job to never  take their eyes off the statue they can  alternate breaks but the statue must  never be allowed to be unobserved for  even a second and because each person  who has seen the statue is a security  risk the d-class agents are equipped  with instant kill devices so they can be  terminated from afar rather than being  potential targets the level 2 agent  meanwhile has a very difficult job this  is one of the most specialized tasks in  the entire foundation because the agent  must be either blind or equipped with a  helmet that completely blocks their  vision which they must wear for their  entire scp-689  shift all control features in the  chamber are designed to be operated by  someone without the ability to see and  the operator is not to remove their  helmet under any circumstances or they  risk termination themselves as a  potential security risk and escape  vector but don't worry even if the  statue still manages to escape its  chamber the foundation has a plan just  don't tell staff assigned to 689 what it  is in the event of a containment breach  or failure of the lights in the statue's  chamber the first priority is to  terminate any d-class or level 1  observers who may have been exposed to  the haunter in the dark this is to  reduce potential targets and while  higher level staff will be retained in  most cases this only goes for the first  containment failure the foundation will  then deploy a retrieval team of blind  agents or those wearing vision blocking  headsets equipped with echolocation tech  they'll partner with d-class observers  to track down everyone who is known to  have viewed the statue the statue will  invariably appear and lead to the death  of one of these people so knowledge of  these potential targets is key to  containment then comes the challenge of  returning it to containment as soon as  the statue is located a perimeter is  established with coverings put up to  avoid any outside viewers catching a  glimpse of it the d-class observers  enter the perimeter and are transported  back to the facility together to ensure  it never falls out of sight until it is  safely back in its chamber and its  containment protocols are put back in  place but what is actually known about  this deadly statue because of how  dangerous and fast-moving the statue is  any attempts to study its properties  must be approved by the presiding  scientists and are carefully scrutinized  the curiosity to figure out its  mysteries is always tempered by the fact  that any scientist interested may be  subject to summary termination should it  breach containment again its origins are  unknown but it is thought to be at least  several centuries old and its form is  believed to be based on a god of the  underworld this would explain its one  function ensuring people make a swift  visit to the afterlife it does not seem  to have any direct hostility towards  humans or scp personnel and has not  given any indication that it is sapient  or intelligent but it does seem to want  to spread as quickly as possible and it  may be able to sense where its best  targets with the greatest potential to  spread are located this has led many to  compare it to one of the scp  foundation's most notorious residents  scp-173 is another statue that poses a  grave danger to anyone who looks at it  the right way similar to  scp-689 it is frozen in place and  requires anyone who enters its  containment unit to look directly at it  any breaking of eye contact can be  deadly and it's more strict in its  definition of breaking eye contact than  689 is simply taking your eyes off for  even a second even to blink is enough to  seal your fate but scp-173 doesn't use  supernatural powers to claim its victim  this large concrete statue instead  becomes mobile and extremely violent  when eye contact is broken killing its  targets by strangulation or breaking the  neck while this entity has killed many  personnel since its containment it  doesn't seem to have the same ability of  scp-689 to teleport to a completely  different location which means it is  actually less of a threat than the  haunter in the dark but the two statues  similar mo of killing when eye contact  is broken has led some to speculate a  connection despite one being of modern  construction and the other being old  possibly even ancient but one of these  statues poses a potential end of the  world scenario which is why the  foundation is so concerned about scp-689  breaching containment  scp-689 might just be among the hardest  anomalies to get back in the bottle once  it escapes if it appears far outside  containment in a crowded scene it now  has hundreds of new potential targets by  the time the foundation tracks it down  to its past location it will have likely  teleported again and there seems to be  no limit to how many lives it can claim  in a set time that means that as it  racks up more targets and teleports into  crowds it could escalate into a major  threat to earth's entire population with  scp-689 seeming to be able to kill  anything that breaks eye contact with it  there are some in the foundation who  wonder if it should be used against the  most notorious captive of the scp  foundation  scp-682  this rage-filled indestructible  regenerating beast has been a thorn in  the foundation side for years it has  cost countless lives of agents and  personnel with its many containment  breaches and so far the foundation has  been unable to terminate it by any  conventional means but scp-689 isn't  exactly what you would call conventional  means it simply triggers an invariably  fatal reaction within the body of  whoever it targets which means it could  possibly be the only thing that could  kill  scp-682 permanently the risks of putting  these two anomalies against each other  are immense though not only does any  interaction with scp-682 carry risks of  yet another catastrophic containment  breach but moving the volatile  scp-689 puts everyone not just those in  the foundation at risk too the proposed  plan involves exposing the two then  immediately turning off the lights but  for this experiment to be pulled off  safely every personnel who has seen  scp-689 must either be terminated or  placed in the same containment chamber  giving the statue no choice but to  eventually choose as cp 682 to improve  the chance of success the doctors  planning this operation have suggested  terminating all d-class personnel in  advance to better the odds should this  experiment ever be approved though a  failure could be truly catastrophic  scp-682 has already shown itself to be  able to come back from things that are  seemingly impossible to survive  including having the majority of its  body destroyed with only atoms remaining  and yet it was still able to regenerate  back who's to say it couldn't survive a  heart attack or organ rupture too there  is also the risk of 682 gaining the  power used against it the only thing  worse than scp-682  is an scp-682 that can now teleport  around the world to kill anyone who has  ever looked at it but even with these  risks the experiment has not been  officially ruled out could one of the  foundation's deadliest ketter class  anomalies be the solution to another  it's under advisement but for right now  the foundation is keeping a very close  eye on scp-689  in more ways than one for more on the  foundation's first killer statue check  out  scp-173 the sculpture tale or watch  termination attempts scp-682 for just  how hard this lizard is to kill

